resolved_issues.body:
This is pretty straightforward and being followed up by a PR, but essentially, any calls to `mockStatic` skip the `DoNotMockEnforcer` entirely.

```java
@DoNotMock
class TypeAnnotatedWithDoNotMock {}

// This does not throw an exception. Checking the stack, I see that DoNotMockEnforcer is never called.
Mockito.mockStatic(TypeAnnotatedWithDoNotMock.class);
``` 

 - [X] Read the [contributing guide](https://github.com/mockito/mockito/blob/main/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md)

fix_patch:
diff --git a/src/main/java/org/mockito/configuration/DoNotMockEnforcer.java b/src/main/java/org/mockito/configuration/DoNotMockEnforcer.java
index d946af6cf..9c7819d4a 100644
--- a/src/main/java/org/mockito/configuration/DoNotMockEnforcer.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/mockito/configuration/DoNotMockEnforcer.java
@@ -4,20 +4,96 @@
  */
 package org.mockito.configuration;

+import org.mockito.NotExtensible;
+import org.mockito.plugins.enforcers.DoNotMockEnforcerWithType;
+
+import java.util.Set;
+import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;
+
 /**
  * Enforcer that is applied to every type in the type hierarchy of the class-to-be-mocked.
  */
-public interface DoNotMockEnforcer {
+public interface DoNotMockEnforcer extends DoNotMockEnforcerWithType {

     /**
-     * If this type is allowed to be mocked. Return an empty optional if the enforcer allows
+     * Static cache for types that are known to be mockable and
+     * thus may be skipped while traversing the class hierarchy.
